// Description: Detects process executions containing the Windows Search "crumb=location:" parameter that references a UNC network path, which may indicate abuse of Windows Explorer search functionality to access remote shares, deliver malicious content, or facilitate phishing and initial access techniques.
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1204, T1204.002, T1021.002
// Data Sources: DeviceProcessEvents
// Threat Actor: Commonly observed in phishing campaigns, malware delivery operations, and adversary tradecraft leveraging Windows Search and remote network shares; not attributed to a specific actor.
// Severity: Medium
// False Positives: Legitimate searches of corporate file shares, administrative access to network resources, document management systems, file discovery activities, and normal user interactions with Windows Explorer search features.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(30d)
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "crumb=location:"
| where ProcessCommandLine matches regex @"\\\\[^\\]+\\"
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceName,
    AccountName,
    FileName,
    ProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine
| order by Timestamp desc
